                <h2>Checklist: Preventing Campaign Disruption from Ad Account Balance Alerts</h2>
<p>Ad account balance management seems straightforward, but insufficient balance causing campaign disruption is one of the most common operational errors in overseas advertising. One outage can cause your high-performing creatives to miss critical scaling windows, directly damaging ROI. This checklist provides five actionable steps with supporting checklist items to help teams establish robust balance management protocols.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Configure Multi-Tier Alert Rules</h2>
<p><strong>Actions:</strong><br />
1. Log into the ad platform backend and access account settings<br />
2. Locate "Budget &amp; Billing" or "Notification Preferences"<br />
3. Configure at least two alert levels:<br />
   - <strong>Tier 1 Alert</strong>: Triggers when balance falls below 3x daily average spend, indicating "monitor closely"<br />
   - <strong>Tier 2 Alert</strong>: Triggers when balance falls below 1.5x daily average spend, indicating "act immediately"<br />
   - <strong>Urgent Alert</strong>: Triggers when balance falls below maximum single-day spend, indicating "imminent disruption"<br />
4. Enable at least two notification methods: email + SMS or instant messaging<br />
5. Assign on-duty performance marketers as notification recipients</p>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong><br />
- [ ] Three-tier thresholds calibrated based on actual spend data<br />
- [ ] At least two notification channels active<br />
- [ ] All relevant personnel added to notification list<br />
- [ ] Alert testing verified for normal receipt</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Establish Daily Balance Check SOP</h2>
<p><strong>Actions:</strong><br />
1. Check all active account balances at fixed times (recommended: 10:00 AM and 4:00 PM Beijing time)<br />
2. Record daily spend rate and estimate remaining campaign days<br />
3. If remaining days &lt; 3, flag as "pending recharge"<br />
4. Maintain balance management log including: account name, current balance, daily average spend, estimated outage time</p>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong><br />
- [ ] Daily check times solidified into workflow<br />
- [ ] Balance log template created and shared with team<br />
- [ ] "Pending recharge" flags have assigned follow-up owners<br />
- [ ] Historical spend data traceable for trend analysis</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Prepare Multiple Recharge Channels</h2>
<p><strong>Actions:</strong><br />
1. List supported recharge methods: credit card, bank transfer, agency recharge, digital wallet, etc.<br />
2. Evaluate processing speeds:<br />
   - Credit card/digital wallet: usually instant<br />
   - Bank transfer: 1-3 business days<br />
   - Agency recharge: varies from hours to 1 day<br />
3. Complete credential verification in advance to avoid KYC delays during urgent recharges<br />
4. Establish recharge priority list: primary channel A, backup channel B</p>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong><br />
- [ ] Primary recharge channel verification completed<br />
- [ ] Account payment information saved for quick operations<br />
- [ ] Agency recharge contact added to emergency contacts<br />
- [ ] All channel processing times recorded, team informed</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Emergency Response for Unexpected Outages</h2>
<p><strong>Actions:</strong><br />
1. Upon discovering account suspension, confirm whether cause is insufficient balance<br />
2. Simultaneously initiate recharge process, prioritizing instant channels<br />
3. After recharge, verify ad status and manually resume paused campaigns<br />
4. Record outage duration and affected scope</p>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong><br />
- [ ] Emergency contact list updated<br />
- [ ] Instant channel payment methods readily available<br />
- [ ] Post-recharge ad status confirmed to prevent auto-pause without recovery<br />
- [ ] Outage event recorded with timeline and processing duration</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 5: Post-Incident Review and Threshold Optimization</h2>
<p><strong>Actions:</strong><br />
1. Monthly summary of all balance alerts and outage events<br />
2. Analyze spend rate fluctuation causes: campaign bid adjustments, creative fatigue, new campaign ramp-up, etc.<br />
3. Adjust alert thresholds based on review findings to better match reality<br />
4. Add typical cases to team knowledge base as onboarding materials</p>
<p><strong>Checklist:</strong><br />
- [ ] Monthly review records archived<br />
- [ ] Alert thresholds updated based on data<br />
- [ ] Knowledge base populated with outage handling cases<br />
- [ ] New accounts have complete alert configuration checklist</p>
